<speak>Yes, clear routing can make routine assistance less frustrating. We can identify the appropriate contact for the particular administrative question when it arises, rather than sending you through several general conversations. I will keep today's housekeeping notes concise and separate from the formal record of the main discussion. You do not need to reproduce your whole filing story again next time merely to explain why clear correspondence matters to you. For now, I have no further questions about your office routine or travel arrangements. We can bring the main part of today's call together and then leave you to return to your afternoon.</speak>